# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Command Center — environment
#
# Every variable here is read on the server only. The browser talks exclusively
# to this app's own /api routes, so no provider key and no home address is ever
# included in a client bundle. Nothing in this file is required: with an empty
# .env the app serves real weather, real radar and real alerts, and says
# plainly which modules it cannot reach.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Weather, radar and alerts ---------------------------------------------
# Forecast (Open-Meteo), radar (RainViewer) and severe-weather alerts (National
# Weather Service) all need no key at all, so these modules work out of the box.
#
# NWS asks API consumers to identify themselves so they can contact the operator
# of a misbehaving client. Set this to something that reaches you. The same
# string is sent to Nominatim, whose usage policy asks for the same.
NWS_USER_AGENT="CommandCenter (you@example.com)"

# Optional commercial weather providers. Not currently used for the forecast —
# Open-Meteo covers it keylessly — but read by lib/env.ts so a provider can be
# added without touching configuration plumbing.
OPENWEATHER_API_KEY=
TOMORROW_API_KEY=
WEATHERAPI_KEY=

# --- Traffic and routing ---------------------------------------------------
# Set ONE of these for traffic-aware drive times. Without any of them the app
# still routes, using OSRM's public server, but on free-flow times only: the
# delay is reported as unavailable rather than as zero, and the UI says so.
#
# Preference order is Mapbox, then HERE, then Google.
MAPBOX_TOKEN=
HERE_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# --- Road conditions -------------------------------------------------------
# PennDOT 511PA developer key, for closures, construction and restrictions.
# Without it the road-conditions module reports that it is not configured —
# it never reports that the roads are clear.
PENNDOT_API_KEY=
# Override if 511PA move their event endpoint.
PENNDOT_EVENTS_URL=

# --- Locations -------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults are the Avondale, PA 19311 borough centroid for home and the
# JPMorgan Chase campus at 500 Stein Christiana Road, Newark, DE for work.
#
# HOME_LAT/HOME_LON deliberately default to the town rather than a street
# address: the weather is identical either way and the town reveals less. Set
# them only if you want the route to start closer to your door.
HOME_LAT=
HOME_LON=
HOME_LABEL=
# Read on the server to build the commute route. Never sent to the browser and
# never sent to a geocoder.
HOME_ADDRESS=

WORK_LAT=
WORK_LON=
WORK_LABEL=
# Geocoded to verify the destination; the coordinates above are the fallback.
WORK_ADDRESS=

# --- Privacy ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Set this before putting the app anywhere publicly reachable. With a passcode
# configured, the commute route and road conditions are withheld until it is
# entered — the route traces the line from your home to your desk.
COMMAND_CENTER_PASSCODE=

# --- Development -----------------------------------------------------------
# Serves labelled sample data for every module that can honestly be simulated,
# for UI work with no network. Weather, air quality and routing are simulated
# and badged DEMO DATA. Severe-weather alerts, radar imagery and public-safety
# announcements are never simulated, because a convincing fake of any of those
# is indistinguishable from the real thing on screen.
DEMO_MODE=
